UPDATE companies SET description='Pascagoula Sheet Metal Works traces its roots to 1944 when Lawrence Hill and Sons Roofing and Sheet Metal opened in Pascagoula, Mississippi. The business was incorporated under its current name in 1967 and has remained family‑owned through three generations; it is now woman‑owned and operated.

The shop focuses on custom sheet metal fabrication for industrial customers along the Mississippi Gulf Coast. The facility operates Monday through Thursday, 7:00 a.m. to 5:30 p.m., though square footage and headcount are not disclosed.

Concrete examples from recent work include a stainless‑steel motor shroud remake, marine duct made for confined spaces, a vortex breaker, and an aluminum filter rack housing.

The company emphasizes its deep local history—over 50 years on the Gulf Coast—and its continuity as a family‑run, woman‑led operation as the foundation of its service approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Perforating", "Marine duct fabrication", "Vortex breaker fabrication", "Aluminum filter rack housing fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Marine"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated for three generations", "Woman-owned and operated", "Over 50 years serving the Mississippi Gulf Coast", "Custom sheet metal fabrication for industrial sector", "Perforating capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1944 as Lawrence Hill and Sons Roofing and Sheet Metal -> /about-us", "Incorporated 1967 as Pascagoula Sheet Metal Works -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated for three generations -> /about-us", "Now woman-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Located at 5609 Veteran''s St., Pascagoula, MS 39581 -> /", "Specializes in custom sheet metal fabrication for industrial sector -> /about-us", "Capability to perforate material as needed -> /", "Products: motor shroud remade into stainless steel, marine duct, vortex breaker, aluminum filter rack housing -> /", "Serving Mississippi Gulf Coast for over 50 years -> /", "Hours: Monday-Thursday 7:00am-5:30pm -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Pascagoula Sheet Metal specializes in custom sheet metal fabrication in the industrial sector for the Mississippi Gulf Coast.", "founded_year": "1944", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pascagoula-sheet-metal-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Harold Lempka opened Minden Machine Shop in 1984 in Minden, Nebraska, starting in a 30-by-50-foot building along the railroad tracks with an old lathe and welder. What began as a side venture with a partner soon became a full-time operation; after the partner departed, Harold''s sons Larry and Kerry joined the business, turning it into a family-run enterprise.

In 1994 the company branded its own line of farm equipment as Patriot Equipment, reflecting the founders'' sense of patriotism. The operation moved to its current site in 1995 and has grown to more than 92,000 square feet of manufacturing space with over 60 employees. Today Patriot Equipment produces 31 distinct equipment lines—seed tenders alone come in ten size and style variations—while still operating a job-shop division that repairs machinery for farmers, commercial clients, schools, and hospitals.

Custom fabrication work ranges from steel bridges and amphitheaters to smaller metal art and hydraulic assemblies.

The company attributes its steady growth to a philosophy set by Harold Lempka: do a good job at a fair price and treat every customer with respect. That principle, combined with in-house capabilities from laser cutting and robotic welding to engine and hydraulic assembly, underpins the Patriot Equipment brand.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Drafting", "Laser cutting", "Metal bending", "Material sawing", "Robotic welding", "Hand welding", "Painting", "Router table cutting", "Assembly", "Electrical work", "Small engine assembly", "Large engine assembly", "Hydraulics assembly", "Steel fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Aluminum fabrication"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Commercial", "Education", "Healthcare"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"Helping Farmers Feed America\" mission guiding product development", "31 equipment lines with multiple variations per line", "Family ownership spanning two generations", "Combined OEM manufacturing and custom repair/fabrication services", "In-house capabilities from laser cutting to hydraulic assembly"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 by Harold Lempka in Minden, Nebraska -> /about-us", "Started in 30x50 ft building with lathe and welder -> /about-us", "Branded Patriot Equipment in 1994 -> /about-us", "Moved to current location in 1995 -> /about-us", "Facility now >92,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Manufactures 31 lines of equipment -> /about-us", "Seed tenders have 10 variations -> /about-us", "Employee count >60 (19 in 2004, 30 in 2008) -> /about-us", "Family-owned (Harold, sons Larry and Kerry) -> /about-us", "Does custom manufacturing and repair -> /services", "Capabilities: Drafting, Laser Cutting, Metal Bending, Material Sawing, Robotic Welding, Hand Welding, Painting, Router Table Cutting, Assembly, Electrical, Small Engine, Large Engine, Hydraulics -> /services", "Materials: Steel, Stainless Steel, Aluminum -> /services", "Serves farmers, companies, schools, hospitals -> /about-us", "Philosophy: good job at fair price, treat customer with respect -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufacturing high quality agriculture machinery and equipment", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "60+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='patriot-equipment-minden-machine-shop-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Patton Electronics Co. is headquartered in Gaithersburg, Maryland. The company presents itself as a multi-national organization that designs, develops, and manufactures network access, connectivity, voice-over-IP, high availability, triple play, and video surveillance equipment for carrier, enterprise, and industrial networks worldwide. No founding year, ownership structure, or founder names are disclosed in the available sources.

The company delivers complete embedded system solutions spanning feasibility analysis, hardware definition, software architecture, development, verification, and commissioning. It also provides project and program management services including budget development, scheduling, and go-to-market strategy. Manufacturing capacity ranges from low-volume original design manufacturing and distribution (ODMD) with minimum order quantities as low as one unit and estimated annual usage in the hundreds, through to high-volume production ramp. A Special Projects Group (SPG) offers custom engineering, dedicated facilities, and project execution services. Support tiers include Level 1/2/3 assistance, 24x7 premium support, warranty programs, software upgrades, and RMA processing.

Patton serves telecommunications carriers, enterprise IT, industrial automation, defense and security agencies, power utilities, emergency communications providers, and broadcast/media operations. Concrete engagements include a U.S. defense subcontract for source-secure fiber optic modules, a partnership with alfanar to secure Saudi power infrastructure, collaboration with XOP Networks on secure IP/SIP emergency communications, and a data diode kit with NSA-listed security developed with Probity for critical infrastructure protection. The Artel brand addresses broadcast transport with 12G-SDI fiber extenders and PTP switches.

The company emphasizes U.S. manufacturing, a full-stack embedded development model, and the ability to support both low-volume custom ODMD programs and high-volume production from the same organization.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Embedded hardware design and development", "Embedded software architecture and development", "Feasibility and cost analysis", "Project planning and resource management", "Verification, commissioning and acceptance testing", "Project and program management", "Budget development and schedule generation", "Go-to-market strategy consultancy", "Original Design Manufacturing and Distribution (ODMD)", "Low-volume manufacturing (MOQ 1)", "High-volume production ramp", "Level 1/2/3 technical support", "24x7 premium support", "Warranty services and extended warranties", "Software upgrades and maintenance", "Returns and RMA processing", "Special projects and custom solutions"], "industries": ["Telecommunications carriers", "Enterprise networks", "Industrial automation", "Defense and security", "Power and utilities infrastructure", "Emergency communications", "Broadcast and media production", "Critical infrastructure protection"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low volume (100s annually) to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S.-manufactured network equipment", "Minimum order quantity as low as 1 unit", "Low-volume ODMD with ramp to high-volume production", "Full embedded hardware/software design, development, and distribution", "Special Projects Group for custom engineering and dedicated facilities", "24x7 premium support with Level 1/2/3 technical assistance"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Gaithersburg, Maryland -> db", "Designs, develops, manufactures network access, VoIP, video surveillance equipment -> /capabilities", "Embedded system capabilities: feasibility, hardware/software development, verification -> /capabilities", "Project management services: budget, schedule, go-to-market strategy -> /capabilities", "High volume capacity and low volume capability, MOQ as low as 1, annual usage in 100s -> /capabilities", "ODMD: Original Design, Manufacturing and Distribution -> /capabilities", "Level 1/2/3 support, 24x7 premium support -> /services", "Special Projects Group (SPG) with services, projects, facilities -> /capabilities", "Products: VoIP adapters, gateways, routers, IADs, SBCs, media gateways, SS7 gateways, SIP phones -> /", "Industrial switches, PoE switches, Ethernet extenders -> /", "xDSL products, DSL modems -> /", "Fiber serial datacom (RS-232/422/530/188C) -> /", "Fiber telecom (T1/E1/PRI, Analog & ISDN) -> /", "Defense/Security fiber communications -> /", "Media transport: video over IP/fiber, Artel racks & chassis -> /", "U.S. defense subcontract for source-secure fiber optic modules -> /", "Partnership with alfanar for Saudi power infrastructure -> /", "Partnership with XOP Networks for secure IP/SIP emergency communications -> /", "Data diode kit with NSA-listed security with Probity -> /", "US-manufactured 12G-SDI fiber extender kits -> /", "International sales/support contacts (US, Hungary, Switzerland) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Patton is a multi-national organization that designs, develops, and manufactures network access, connectivity, voice-over-IP, high availability, triple play, and video surveillance equipment for carrier, enterprise, and industrial networks worldwide.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='patton-electronics-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Patton''s Medical, based in Charlotte, North Carolina, traces its roots to 1980 when Pattons Inc. began selling custom medical air packages to hospitals. The current entity, Pattons Medical, was established in 2008 to sell and service proprietary medical gas equipment nationwide. In 2012, ELGi USA acquired the company to enter the U.S. medical equipment market and diversify its industrial product portfolio.

The company designs and assembles medical air systems using Hitachi oil-less reciprocating scroll compressors in base-mount, modular, and tank-mounted configurations. It also provides medical vacuum systems built around Busch oil-less, contactless multi-claw pumps suited for waste anesthetic gas disposal (WAGD) applications. In addition, Patton''s Medical supplies pipeline products — including manifolds, outlets, zone valves, alarms, and architectural components — through strategic partnerships, and engineers laboratory air and pipeline systems for research and academic facilities. The firm offers custom package engineering, installation, and ongoing service for all equipment it sells.

Primary customers include hospitals, clinical laboratories, and universities across the United States. The company''s laboratory team specifically targets lab and university clients for air and pipeline systems, while its medical air and vacuum packages serve healthcare facilities requiring NFPA 99-compliant gas delivery.

Patton''s Medical emphasizes its ability to develop custom medical gas packages when standard products do not meet a facility''s specifications. It highlights compliance with NFPA 99 standards and UL 508A-listed control panels, a nationwide service network, and long-standing partnerships that bring technologically advanced pipeline components to its offerings. The company describes its founding principle as an "old fashion" commitment to customer service backed by deep product knowledge.', certifications=ARRAY['NFPA 99','UL 508A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical air system design and assembly", "Medical vacuum system design and assembly", "Pipeline product supply and integration", "Laboratory air system design", "Medical gas equipment installation", "Medical gas equipment service and maintenance", "Custom medical gas package engineering", "NFPA 99 compliance consulting"], "industries": ["Healthcare (hospitals)", "Clinical laboratories", "Universities and research institutions"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Hitachi oil-less reciprocating scroll compressors", "Busch multi-claw vacuum pumps"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Products meet or exceed NFPA 99 standards", "Control panels UL 508A approved", "Custom medical gas packages engineered to specification", "Partnerships for advanced pipeline products (outlets, zone valves, alarms, manifolds)", "Nationwide sales and service of proprietary medical gas equipment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Charlotte, North Carolina -> db", "Founded 2008 (Pattons Medical) -> /", "Predecessor Pattons Inc. began 1980 -> /", "Acquired by ELGi USA in 2012 -> /", "Medical air systems with Hitachi compressors -> /", "Medical vacuum systems with Busch pumps -> /", "Pipeline products via partnerships -> /", "Laboratory air systems for labs and universities -> /", "NFPA 99 and UL 508A compliance -> /", "Custom package engineering -> /", "Installation and service offerings -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Deciding to sell and service our own medical gas equipment nationwide, we created Pattons Medical in 2008. This does not mean Pattons Medical is the \"new kid on the block.\" We hired some of the best in the medical gas business with extensive backgrounds in sales, marketing, manufacturing and engineering. Within a short period of time, we were able to create a company and product line that is second to none in the industry.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='patton-s-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Paul Renwick Textiles is based in New York, New York. After creating patterns and products for some of the world’s fashion houses, Renwick developed a command of scale, rhythm, and ornament that now defines his hand-embroidered textiles.

The studio produces hand-embroidered textiles using vegetable-dyed threads on organic linen and cotton. Each piece is meticulously handcrafted in partnership with a dedicated workroom in Nepal, where Renwick oversees every stitch.

The textiles serve interior design projects and fashion houses, with designs suited for both sleek urban apartments and storied country houses.

Renwick grounds the work in personal expression and a lifelong passion for the decorative arts, rejecting trends in favor of patient, deliberate artistry. The brand’s differentiators include a commitment to integrity, vegetable-dyed materials, and the oversight of a Nepalese workroom that ensures each stitch meets exacting standards.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand embroidery", "Textile design", "Custom textile design", "Vegetable dyeing", "Organic linen and cotton sourcing"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Vegetable-dyed threads", "Organic linen", "Organic cotton"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-embroidered textiles crafted in a dedicated Nepalese workroom", "Vegetable-dyed threads on organic linen and cotton", "Designer background with leading fashion houses", "Commitment to patient, deliberate artistry over trends"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: New York, New York -> db", "Founder: Paul Renwick -> /about", "Scottish designer with decades of experience -> /about", "Background in fashion ateliers and interior projects -> /about", "Created patterns for leading fashion houses -> /about", "Produces hand-embroidered textiles -> /about", "Partnership with workroom in Nepal -> /about", "Uses vegetable-dyed threads -> /about", "Uses organic linen and cotton -> /about", "Emphasis on personal expression over trends -> /about", "Commitment to integrity and patient artistry -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "In partnership with a devoted workroom in Nepal, he oversees the meticulous handcrafting of each piece.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paul-renwick-textiles' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Payoff Solar is based in South Jordan, Utah, and was founded in 2024 by Matt Newman, JD McBride, and Kip Denning. The company began with a mission to make solar energy accessible, affordable, and hassle-free for homeowners and businesses, focusing on a financial payoff within three to four years rather than the industry-typical 15 to 20.

The company supplies high-efficiency solar panels and advanced battery storage systems, and provides full-service installation that covers consultation, site assessment, system design, permitting, and final inspection. Pricing is advertised at $1.50 per watt, roughly half the $3–4 per watt commonly quoted by other installers, and customers can choose to perform some of the work themselves to reduce cost further.

Payoff Solar serves residential and commercial customers seeking to reduce energy bills and carbon footprint. Its process is structured in three steps: a quick property and needs assessment, a detailed proposal with specifications and projected savings, and professional installation handled from permits through inspection.

Core values cited are innovation, sustainability, and affordability, with an emphasis on flexible financing and competitive pricing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design", "Solar panel installation", "Battery energy storage installation", "Permitting and inspection management", "Site assessment and consultation", "Ongoing maintenance"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pricing at $1.50 per watt, less than half the typical $3\u20134 per watt", "Target financial payoff in 3\u20134 years versus industry 15\u201320 years", "Option for customers to self-perform portions of the install to save money", "Full-service scope from consultation and design through permitting and inspection"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2024 -> /about", "Headquarters South Jordan, Utah -> db", "Founders Matt Newman, JD McBride, Kip Denning -> /about", "Mission: make solar accessible, affordable, hassle-free -> /about and /", "Focus on 3-4 year financial payoff vs 15-20 industry standard -> /", "Pricing $1.50 per watt vs $3-4 per watt -> /", "Products: high-efficiency solar panels, advanced battery solutions -> / and /about", "Services: consultation, design, installation, permits, inspection, maintenance -> / and /about", "Three-step process: assess, propose, install -> /", "Serves homeowners and businesses -> /about", "Values: innovation, sustainability, affordability -> /about", "Matt Newman 15+ years renewable energy experience -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our professional team handles the entire installation process, from permits to final inspection.", "founded_year": "2024", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() 