UPDATE companies SET description='Performance Systems Integration, doing business as PSI Conversions, operates from Brick Township, New Jersey. The company’s origins trace back more than two decades to the development of its first standalone wiring harness for LS engine swaps, built on a combined 25-plus years of automotive electrical experience.

PSI designs and manufactures plug-and-play wiring harnesses for General Motors Gen II through Gen V LS and LT engines, including the LT1/LT4, LS1/LS6, Vortec, LS2, LS3, LS7, and LT/Ecotec3 families. Harnesses are assembled in-house using high-temperature cross-linked TXL or GXL wire, ultrasonic-welded splices, fusible-link protection, and OEM-specification terminals from suppliers such as Delphi/Aptiv, Yazaki, and Kostal. Each harness is wrapped in high-temp tape and either F6 PET braid or nylon split loom, then 100% functionally tested on computer-controlled Dynalab or Cirris equipment. Beyond harnesses, PSI supplies engine controller kits, transmission components, fuel systems, gauge clusters, and a curated selection of partner brands including Holley, Vintage Air, Dakota Digital, and HPTuners.

The company serves the automotive aftermarket, targeting professional installers, restoration shops, and individual builders performing LS/LT swaps into a wide range of platforms—Chevrolet, Ford, Nissan, Jeep, Toyota, and classic hot rods. A dealer program extends reach to retail and installation partners.

PSI emphasizes domestic production, rapid fulfillment (in-stock harnesses ship in one to three business days), and direct technical support available five days a week by phone and 24/7 by email. The original harness layout, developed for simplified ground and power routing, has become a de facto standard in the LS-swap community.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wiring harness manufacturing", "Ultrasonic wire welding", "High-temp cross-linked wire assembly (TXL/GXL)", "Fusible link wire integration", "High-temp tape and loom application (F6 PET braid, nylon split loom)", "OEM-spec terminal crimping (Delphi/Aptiv, Yazaki, Kostal)", "100% functional testing (Dynalab/Cirris)", "Engine controller kit assembly", "PCM programming", "Technical support for LS/LT swaps", "Fuel system kit assembly", "Gauge cluster integration", "Transmission harness fabrication", "Custom adapter and extension harnesses"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Performance engine swaps", "Hot rod and restoration", "Off-road vehicles"], "materials": ["TXL wire", "GXL wire", "High-temp heat shrink", "Fusible link wire", "High-temp tape", "F6 PET braid", "Nylon split loom", "Delphi/Aptiv terminals", "Yazaki terminals", "Kostal terminals"], "equipment": ["Dynalab test equipment", "Cirris test equipment", "Ultrasonic wire welder"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1-3 business days for in-stock harnesses; extended lead times possible due to demand", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made in the USA with high-temp TXL/GXL wire and OEM-spec terminals", "100% computer-tested on Dynalab or Cirris equipment", "In-stock harnesses ship in 1\u20133 business days", "Ultrasonic-welded splices with high-temp heat shrink", "Direct technical support by phone (Mon\u2013Fri) and email 24/7"], "facts_used": ["Location: Brick Township, New Jersey -> /", "Origins: first standalone harness created over 20 years ago, combined 25+ years experience -> /", "Products: LS/LT swap wiring harnesses f