UPDATE companies SET description='Petoskey Plastics operates from its corporate headquarters in McKinney, Texas, but traces its roots to Petoskey, Michigan, where Duke and Paul Keiswetter founded the company in 1969. The privately held, family-owned business began with five employees and a single bag machine converting purchased film into plastic bags. By 1975 the founders had added an extrusion line to produce their own film, setting the stage for a vertically integrated operation that now spans four U.S. manufacturing sites.

Today the company runs facilities in Petoskey, Michigan; Morristown, Tennessee; Hartford City, Indiana; and McKinney, Texas, employing roughly 500 associates. Its core processes include 3- and 5-layer blown film extrusion, bag converting, shrink film production, and a 330,000-square-foot recycling plant in Indiana that feeds post-consumer resin back into the extrusion lines. A 4-color offset paper printing press at the Morristown site adds packaging capabilities. In-house quality labs at each location support consistent output.

Petoskey serves automotive, construction, medical, retail, institutional, packaging, janitorial, parks and recreation, and fundraising markets, with products sold in 45 countries. Customers range from private-label brands to OEMs seeking custom-engineered polyethylene solutions, including films with up to 70 percent third-party certified post-consumer recycled content that exceed EPA requirements.

The company’s differentiation rests on its closed-loop recycling model, veteran-owned status, and a family-culture that emphasizes hands-on management. After receiving the National Veteran Business Development Council’s Veteran Business of the Year award in 2023 and 2025, Petoskey continues to position its sustainable polyethylene as a lower-carbon alternative for flexible packaging.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polyethylene film extrusion (3-layer, 5-layer)", "Custom plastic bag converting", "Shrink film manufacturing", "Post-consumer plastic recycling (wash line, reprocessing)", "Blown film extrusion", "Converting (bag making, sealing)", "Offset printing (4-color paper)", "Custom-engineered polyethylene solutions", "In-house quality testing and labs"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Construction", "Home Improvement", "Medical", "Retail", "Institutional", "Packaging", "Janitorial", "Parks & Recreation", "Fundraising", "Recycling & Closed Loop", "Private Brand"], "materials": ["Polyethylene", "Post-consumer recycled polyethylene (up to 70%)", "Recycled plastic resin"], "equipment": ["3-layer extrusion lines", "5-layer extrusion lines", "Recycle line (from Italy)", "Wash line technology for post-consumer bags and film", "Blown film manufacturing lines", "Converting lines", "4-color offset paper printing press"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated recycling and manufacturing across four U.S. sites", "Up to 70% third-party certified post-consumer recycled content in films", "98% of equipment capable of 3- and 5-layer extrusion technology", "In-house quality labs at every production facility", "Family-owned, veteran-owned business with 55-year operating history"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 by Duke and Paul Keiswetter -> /about-us", "Family-owned, privately held -> /about-us", "Headquarters in McKinney, Texas -> db, /about-us", "Four manufacturing facilities (Petoskey MI, Morristown TN, 