UPDATE companies SET description='Plexus Corporation is headquartered in Nampa, Idaho, with a global footprint spanning four continents and manufacturing sites including Appleton, Wisconsin. The company traces its roots to the idea of an integrated group of people working together to solve complex challenges, leveraging nearly 50 years of experience in designing and building printed circuit boards and complex assemblies.

The firm provides end-to-end product realization services — product design and development, new product introduction, contract manufacturing, supply chain management, and sustaining services. Its capabilities include complex high-level assembly, grid automation services, failure analysis at board and system levels, and test strategy development. Manufacturing operations are positioned close to customer end markets worldwide, supported by a central point of contact for streamlined communication.

Customers include Bevi, whose sustainable smart water dispensers are manufactured in Appleton, and a global construction and mining equipment maker for which Plexus produces power inverters for hybrid wheel loaders, bulldozers, and underground electric vehicles.

The company emphasizes a culture of trust, courage, and growth, with values centered on growing people, building belonging, innovating responsibly, delivering excellence, and creating customer success. Differentiators cited include a dedicated Failure Analysis Lab, Class A paint standards for harsh environments, and a collaborative model that extends the customer''s R&D capacity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Design & Development", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Contract Manufacturing", "Supply Chain Solutions", "Sustaining Services", "Failure Analysis (board, sub-assembly, system level)", "Complex High-Level Assembly (HLA)", "Grid Automation Services", "PCB Assembly", "Test Strategy Development", "Design for Excellence (DFX)", "PCB Rework Services", "Life Cycle Assessment", "Product Strategy & Requirements Definition", "Manufacturing Process Optimization"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Healthcare & Life Sciences", "Industrial", "Semiconductor Capital Equipment", "Heavy Equipment / Construction & Mining"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nearly 50 years of PCB design and assembly experience", "Failure Analysis Lab for board, sub-assembly, and system-level root cause analysis", "Global manufacturing footprint across four continents near customer end markets", "Class A paint standards for components in severe environments", "Central point of contact for worldwide program management"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Nampa, Idaho -> db", "Global presence across four continents -> /about", "Manufacturing site in Appleton, WI (Bevi testimonial) -> /about", "Nearly 50 years of PCB design and assembly experience -> /quality", "Failure Analysis Lab for board, sub-assembly, system level -> /quality", "Class A paint standards for harsh environments -> /quality", "Central point of contact for global regions -> /quality", "Industries: Aerospace/Defense, Healthc