UPDATE companies SET description='Popknot Wood operates from Rogers, Arkansas. The business traces its roots to founder John, a U.S. Army veteran, who began teaching his grandchildren woodworking in his shop. What started as birdhouses and simple boxes grew into a family-driven venture; together they built a business plan and launched Popknot Wood. The company is proudly veteran-owned and family-operated.

The shop delivers custom woodworking, furniture restoration, and precision CNC and laser work. Capabilities include custom-built wood products, replacement of broken or discontinued parts, heirloom repairs, and a range of specialty items such as cutting boards (including state-shaped designs), wooden urns and memorial pieces, awards and presentation pieces, river tables, custom flags, and signs. Production is carried out in a small workshop that sources local wood whenever possible and ships finished pieces to all 50 states.

Customers include individuals seeking one-of-a-kind furniture repairs or personalized gifts, families commissioning memorial urns or heirloom restorations, and faith-based organizations such as churches and ministries looking for purpose-built pieces. The shop also serves buyers of awards, presentation items, and custom signage.

John credits his Army service for instilling discipline and integrity that carry into every build. He views craftsmanship as stewardship — using given gifts to create meaningful, lasting work. The business began as a way to teach creativity, responsibility, and entrepreneurship to the next generation, and that legacy remains central to its purpose.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Furniture restoration and repair", "Custom fabrication of wood products", "Replacement of broken or discontinued wood parts", "Heirloom repairs and restorations", "Custom cutting boards", "Wooden urns and memorial pieces", "Awards and presentation pieces", "River tables", "Custom flags and signs", "CNC machining", "Laser engraving and cutting", "Faith-based creations"], "industries": ["Custom woodworking", "Furniture restoration", "Memorial products", "Awards and recognition", "Faith-based products", "Home goods", "Signage"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned and family-driven operation", "Sources local wood whenever possible", "Ships nationwide to all 50 states", "Faith-informed craftsmanship for homes, churches, and ministries", "Teaches woodworking skills across generations"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Rogers, Arkansas -> db", "Founder John is a U.S. Army veteran -> /about", "Company is veteran-owned and family-driven -> /about", "Began as shop projects with grandkids -> /about", "Offers custom woodworking, restoration, CNC and laser work -> /, /about", "Products include cutting boards, urns, awards, river tables, flags, signs -> /", "Ships to all 50 states -> /about", "Uses local wood when possible -> /about", "Faith-based creations for homes, churches, ministries -> /about", "Recognized as Best Woodworker in Rogers, AR (2026) -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in custom woodworking, restoration, and precision-crafted pieces", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='popknot-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Porter Barn Wood operates from Phoenix, Arizona. The business was founded in 2010 by Thomas Porter, who started the venture with the help of his friend Craig Suiter after using a forklift to unload a shipment of reclaimed barn wood and recognizing local demand for such materials. Porter formed the LLC in 2012 and opened a showroom that now serves both walk-in customers and commercial clients.

The company runs a wood shop, metal shop, concrete shop, and finishing/contracting teams, enabling it to fabricate custom furniture, architectural elements, lighting, and millwork. Core processes include CNC plasma cutting, CNC routing, laser engraving, blacksmithing, milling, spindle duplication, and production manufacturing. Design services cover 3D CAD, concept rendering, and furniture design, while finishing options span lacquer, polyurethane, conversion varnish, waxes, oils, and custom finish matching. The facility features evap-cooled and air-conditioned workshops and handles projects ranging from small DIY pieces to large commercial build-outs.

The shop has also hosted film and television productions for HGTV and PBS specials. In addition, the company supplies reclaimed materials to DIY enthusiasts and runs free community classes and demonstrations.

Porter describes the operation as a family business focused on growing while keeping high-quality reclaimed materials at reasonable prices. A stated differentiator is the willingness to incorporate customers'' own reclaimed materials — whether from a family barn, old warehouse, or unique finds — into custom projects, and the ability to provide design, fabrication, and installation under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metalworking", "Blacksmithing", "Furniture fabrication", "Lighting fabrication", "Woodworking", "Milling", "Furniture repair", "Modifications", "Spindle duplication", "Production manufacturing", "CNC plasma cutting", "CNC routing", "Laser engraving", "Architectural photography", "Interior design photography", "Image licensing", "Custom finishing (lacquer, polyurethane, conversion varnish, waxes, oils, custom finish matching)", "3D CAD design", "Concept rendering", "Furniture design"], "industries": ["Restaurant", "Hospitality", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Interior design", "Architecture", "Film and television production"], "materials": ["Reclaimed barn wood", "Mushroom wood", "Hand-hewn beams", "Live edge slabs", "Salvaged lumber (from forest fires, controlled burns, beetle-killed trees)", "Pallet wood", "Metal sheeting", "Glass", "Concrete", "Leather", "Plastic", "Styrofoam", "Acrylic"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma cutter", "CNC router", "Laser engraver", "Forklift"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combines traditional craftsmanship with modern CNC capabilities for one-offs and production runs", "Accepts and incorporates customer-supplied reclaimed materials into projects", "Offers free woodworking and metalworking classes and demonstrations", "Provides TV-friendly shop facilities for film and television productions", "Operates wood, metal, concrete, and finishing shops under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 by Thomas Porter -> /about", "LLC formed in 2012 with help from Craig Suiter -> /about-us", "Located in Phoenix, Arizona -> db, /about-us", "Operates wood, metal, concrete, and finishing shops -> /", "Processes: CNC plasma, CNC routing, laser engraving, blacksmithing, milling, spindle duplication, production manufacturing -> /services", "Design services: 3D CAD, concept rendering, furniture design -> /services", "Finishing options: lacquer, polyurethane, conversion varnish, waxes, oils, custom finish matching -> /services", "Serves restaurants (Surf City, Lazy Bird, Fam\u00e8), hospitality, commercial, residential, architects, builders -> /", "Hosts film/TV productions (HGTV, PBS) -> /", "Offers free classes and demonstrations -> /", "Works with customer-supplied reclaimed materials -> /", "Materials: reclaimed barn wood, mushroom wood, hand-hewn beams, live edge slabs, salvaged lumber, pallet wood, metal, glass, concrete, leather, plastic, styrofoam, acrylic -> /, /about-us", "Equipment: CNC plasma cutter, CNC router, laser engraver, forklift -> /services, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "With a wood shop, metal shop, concrete shop, and finish and contracting teams at our disposal, we fabricate projects of all kinds.", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='porter-barn-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Portsmouth Fabric Company has operated in the historic downtown district of Portsmouth, New Hampshire since 1980, after its founding in 1979 as a source for natural-fiber fabrics, fashion fabrics, and designer cuts. The shop moved to its current location a year after opening and began featuring Bernina sewing machines in 1980, expanding into contemporary quilting fabrics and fiber-arts books in 1990. Today the inventory spans more than 7,000 bolts of fabric.

The store stocks a broad range of textiles including contemporary quilting cottons, Bali batiks, silk dupioni, silk noil, silk organza, silk charmeuse, flannels, batiste, cotton solids, laminates, linens, velvets, and wool. It is an authorized Bernina dealer offering the full line of Swiss-made machines — from the Liberty 495 and 580 to the 770 Plus, 990, and Q-Series longarms — with free, unlimited guide classes and on-site service by a Bernina-trained technician. The shop also carries specialty threads from Aurifil, Isacord, Mettler, and Superior, plus trims, ribbons, buttons, and notions. A dedicated classroom hosts scheduled workshops with visiting artists such as Kaffe Fassett and Brandon Mably, and the space is available for private rental for sewing retreats.

The shop serves the New England quilting and sewing community through two annual clearance events — an Anniversary Sale in early July and a Year-End Clearance in late December — and has supported local charities including New Generation, a shelter for homeless pregnant women.

The company emphasizes professional advice and individualized product selection, a service model it has maintained for over four decades.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabric retail", "Bernina sewing machine sales", "Bernina sewing machine service and repair", "Sewing and quilting classes", "Workshop hosting with visiting artists", "Classroom rental for sewing retreats", "Specialty thread sales", "Notions and trim sales"], "industries": ["Quilting", "Sewing", "Fiber arts", "Textile retail", "Home sewing"], "materials": ["Contemporary quilting cottons", "Bali batik cottons", "Bali batik rayons", "Silk dupioni", "Silk noil", "Silk organza", "Silk charmeuse", "Flannels", "Batiste", "Cotton solids", "Laminates", "Linens", "Velvets", "Wool"], "equipment": ["Bernina 990", "Bernina 770 Plus", "Bernina Liberty 580", "Bernina Liberty 495", "Bernina Q24 longarm", "Bernina Q20 longarm", "Bernina Q16 longarm", "Bernina 215"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the largest and most unique fabric selections in New England with over 7,000 bolts in stock", "Free, unlimited Bernina guide classes with machine purchase", "Classroom available for rent for sewing retreats and private groups", "Two annual clearance sales: Anniversary Sale in July and Year-End Clearance in December/January", "Hosts workshops with internationally known quilters such as Kaffe Fassett and Brandon Mably"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 -> /about-us", "Moved to present location 1980 -> /about-us", "Added contemporary quilting fabrics 1990 -> /about-us", "Inventory over 7,000 bolts -> /about-us", "Located in historic downtown Portsmouth, NH -> /about-us", "Authorized Bernina dealer -> /about-us", "Free unlimited guide classes with Bernina purchase -> /about-us", "Bernina trained technician on site -> /about-us", "Carries Aurifil, Isacord, Mettler, Superior threads -> /about-us", "Classroom available for rent -> /about-us", "Hosts workshops with K