UPDATE companies SET description='Power Factor was founded in March 2013 in Baltimore, Maryland, by master electrician George Lang IV. After graduating from Eastern Vocational Technical High School in 1995 and completing an apprenticeship with Associated Builders and Contractors, Lang ran the electrical maintenance department at Johns Hopkins Hospital before joining a Maryland solar firm as a partner. There he designed a Positive Train Control system and a patented battery system deployed in war zones for the U.S. military. When that company was sold, Lang brought five key employees with him to launch Power Factor as a family-owned solar and electrical contractor.

The company provides full-service solar and electrical installation, repair, replacement, and maintenance for residential, commercial, and industrial properties. With over 60 employees and $18 million in annual sales, Power Factor has completed more than 2,100 residential installations and deployed over 43 megawatts of solar capacity across the United States and abroad.

Customers include homeowners throughout the Baltimore region, businesses seeking to reduce energy costs, and federal agencies — notably the Department of Defense, for which the firm has delivered over 35 megawatts of PV projects. The company also serves the telecommunications sector and works on commercial solar developments nationwide.

Lang started Power Factor to bring reliable, transparent solar and electrical services to communities, drawing on his experience building mission-critical power systems for the military. The company emphasizes no hidden fees, 24/7 emergency response, and NABCEP-certified technicians, aiming to complete every project on time and on budget.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certification','OSHA Certification','Master Electrician License (5 states)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system installation", "Commercial solar array installation", "Residential solar panel installation", "Electrical maintenance and repair", "Battery storage system deployment", "Positive Train Control (PTC) systems", "EV charging station installation", "LEED-certified lighting retrofits", "General electrical construction", "Project management", "Commercial solar development", "Telecommunications infrastructure"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Military/Defense (DOD)", "Telecommunications", "Renewable Energy/Solar"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules", "Battery storage systems", "Electrical conduit and wiring"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 2,100 residential installations; over 43 MW solar deployed", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No hidden fees", "24/7 emergency service", "NABCEP-certified technicians", "OSHA-certified installation crews", "Family-owned with 60+ employees and 43MW+ solar deployed"], "facts_used": ["Founded March 2013 by George Lang IV -> /about", "Family-owned, 60+ employees, $18M annual sales -> /about", "2,100+ residential installations, 43MW+ solar deployed -> /about", "OSHA-certified crews, NABCEP certification -> /about", "No hidden fees, 24/7 emergency service -> /", "Services: solar installation, electrical maintenance, battery systems, EV charging, lighting retrofits -> /, /about", "Industries: residential, commercial, industrial, military/DOD, telecommunications -> /about", "Headquarters: Baltimore, Maryland -> db, /about", "Founder background: Eastern Vocational Technical High School 1995, Johns Hopkins, master electrician 2004 -> /about", "BBB A+ rating -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Power Factor is an electrical and solar company that has been serving the Baltimore area and beyond since 2013.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "60+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='power-factor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Power-Flo Technologies, headquartered in New Hyde Park, New York, traces its roots to 1929. The business operates as a family of companies that includes distributors, fabricators, manufacturers, and motor and pump repair firms serving New York, New Jersey, and New England.

The company distributes over two million electrical and plumbing products from dozens of manufacturers, maintaining a broad warehouse inventory with delivery across the tri-state region. It runs a state-of-the-art repair facility and machine shop capable of servicing motors and pumps from fractional to 1,500 HP at low and medium voltages. In-house fabrication includes UL-certified switchgear and panel building, custom motor controls, and power distribution switchgear design. Diagnostic services cover infrared thermography, vibration analysis, load studies, and power quality analysis. The firm also provides hazardous waste recycling, engineering support, and turnkey energy-efficient lighting upgrades.

Power-Flo serves electrical, institutional, MRO and OEM industrial, plumbing, and mechanical trades. Customers include commercial buildings, public water facilities, and large retailers such as Macy’s Herald Square, which is featured in a case study. Through its sister company US Energy Group, the firm delivers building energy management systems.

