UPDATE companies SET description='PowerFilm Solar operates from Ames, Iowa, where it has designed and manufactured thin-film and crystalline solar panels for over three decades. The company focuses on custom-engineered solar solutions for commercial, government, and OEM platforms, with engineering and production capabilities based in the United States.

The company manufactures thin-film amorphous silicon solar panels using proprietary processes and assembles semi-flexible crystalline panels through controlled production. Its capabilities span panel construction, electrical integration, system-level validation, and full development from prototype through sustained production volumes. PowerFilm supports custom geometry, substrate selection, encapsulation, energy harvesting electronics, charge controllers, and application-specific mounting configurations.

PowerFilm serves commercial transportation fleets seeking to reduce idling and extend battery life for liftgates, telematics, APUs, and refrigeration; government and defense programs requiring portable, vehicle-mounted, and remote power; uncrewed maritime systems needing sealed, marine-grade surface generation; low-speed electric vehicle fleets on campuses and municipal sites; IoT and connected devices in remote environments; and consumer mobility applications. Past deployments include telematics, marine, IoT, U.S. military, and space exploration programs.

The company emphasizes application-specific design over catalog formats, controlled manufacturing with environmental and mechanical testing (vibration, temperature cycling, long-term outdoor exposure), and direct engineering collaboration from early development through deployment. Its U.S.-based thin-film production and crystalline assembly are cited as differentiators for programs requiring domestic sourcing and supply-chain control.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solar panel design and engineering", "Thin-film amorphous silicon manufacturing", "Semi-flexible crystalline solar panel assembly", "Electrical integration (energy harvesting, charge control, regulated outputs)", "System-level integration and validation", "Panel geometry and form factor design", "Substrate selection and encapsulation", "Power management and battery pairing", "Cabling and mounting configuration design", "Environmental testing (vibration, temperature variation, outdoor exposure)", "Prototype development and field testing", "Controlled production and quality assurance", "Design for manufacturability and lifecycle support"], "industries": ["Commercial transportation", "Government and defense", "Uncrewed maritime systems", "Low-speed electric vehicles", "Internet of Things (IoT)", "Consumer mobility", "Telematics", "Marine", "Space exploration"], "materials": ["Amorphous silicon (thin-film)", "Crystalline silicon (semi-flexible)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype through production volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Application-specific design rather than standard product formats", "U.S.-based thin-film amorphous silicon manufacturing", "Controlled production with environmental and mechanical validation", "Engineering collaboration from requirements through sustained production", "Prototype-to-production support for custom solar integration"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Ames, Iowa -> db", "Manufactures thin-film amorphous s