_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='prime-source-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Primitive Precision Metalcraft operates from Minneapolis, Minnesota, where founder Hans Early-Nelson established the shop in 2007. Early-Nelson’s path to metalworking began with a boat-building upbringing, a blacksmithing and furniture-making apprenticeship in Germany, and a welding and machining diploma from Dunwoody Institute of Technology. After working at a stainless-steel fabrication firm, he launched the company to blend old-world craftsmanship with contemporary design. Liz Parent, who holds an art and design degree from the University of Minnesota and spent a decade as a jewelry maker, joined as chief operating officer in 2020, turning a creative partnership into a full-time operation.

The shop specializes in architectural metal fabrication, producing landscape and garden structures, pergolas, countertops, shelving, hardware, functional housewares, feature stairs, handrails, wall coverings, edge details, and kick rails.

The company serves architects, designers, contractors, and homeowners across residential, commercial, and landscape projects in the Twin Cities region.

Early-Nelson founded Primitive Precision to create custom metalwork that matches old-world quality with modern innovative design. The firm emphasizes detailed architectural metalwork and high-quality solutions delivered by a highly talented fabrication team.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural metal fabrication", "Welding", "Machining", "Blacksmithing", "Forging", "Custom metal fabrication", "Structural fabrication", "Decorative metalwork"], "industries": ["Architectural metal fabrication", "Residential metalwork", "Commercial metalwork", "Landscape structures"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom metalwork blending old-world quality with modern design", "Detailed architectural metal fabrication", "Highly skilled in-house fabrication team"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2007 by Hans Early-Nelson -> /about", "Located at 4430 Lyndale Ave N, Minneapolis, MN 55412 -> /, /about", "Architectural metal fabrication -> /", "Projects include landscape structures, countertops, shelving, stairs, handrails, wall coverings -> /", "Hans Early-Nelson background: boat-building, blacksmithing apprenticeship in Germany, welding diploma from Dunwoody Institute of Technology -> /about", "Liz Parent joined in 2020 as COO, art and design degree from University of Minnesota -> /about", "Company focuses on detailed architectural metalwork with talented team -> /about", "Custom metalwork blending old-world quality with modern design -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We do architectural metal fabrication.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='primitive-precision-metalcraft' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Primo Packaging operates from Orlando, Florida, as a manufacturer and converter of custom plastic bags and flexible packaging. The company produces a wide range of bag styles, pouches, and films for diverse end markets.

The facility offers eight-color process printing and multiple lamination methods — solvent, extrusion, dry, and co-extrusion — to create multi-layer structures using materials such as polyethylene, polypropylene, BOPP, CPP, PET, PVDC, and nylon. Capabilities extend to producing three-side-seal pouches, stand-up pouches, flat-bottom pouches, quad-seal bags, wicketed bags, and a long list of standard bag styles including poly mailers, gusseted bags, pallet covers, drum liners, vacuum pouches, and zipper bags. Film formats range from layflat tubing and center-slit gusseted to various sheeting configurations.

Primo Packaging serves industries including confectionery, bakeries, snack foods, pet products, meat and fish processing, agriculture, and landscaping.

