UPDATE companies SET description='Priority Plastics, Inc. is headquartered in Grand Prairie, Texas, and operates extrusion blow-molding manufacturing facilities strategically located across the United States. The company provides plastic packaging solutions with a focus on quality, timeliness, relationships, and sustainability.

The company produces HDPE and PET containers, including PriorityPour tight-head containers, canisters, and dry-pack towel wipes, using extrusion blow molding and injection stretch blow molding (ISBM) processes. Its GreenLite program incorporates post-consumer recycled (PCR) content — up to 80% in ECO multi-layer products — and lightweighting designs. Priority Plastics offers in-plant customer service, custom and stock tooling, labeling capabilities, and multi-plant sourcing from its coast-to-coast footprint, serving customers from startups to multinational firms.

Priority Plastics serves food and beverage, nutrition and wellness, industrial, personal care, agriculture, animal health, cannabis/hemp/CBD, hardware, hazardous materials, healthcare/nutraceutical, and specialty chemicals markets.

The company states its people-centric culture and sustainability commitments drive its differentiation: facilities recycle unused resin, redesign packaging to reduce gram weight, and leverage geographic proximity to lower freight emissions. Published goals include sourcing 60% of materials from recycled or renewable sources by 2035, making 80% of products recyclable by 2028, and cutting Scope 2 and 3 emissions 30% by 2030.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion blow molding", "Injection stretch blow molding (ISBM)", "Custom tooling design and fabrication", "Stock tooling library", "Labeling capabilities", "In-plant customer service support", "Multi-plant sourcing", "GreenLite sustainability program (PCR incorporation, lightweighting)", "PriorityPour tight-head container manufacturing", "Canister manufacturing", "Dry-pack towel wipe packaging", "Multi-layer co-extrusion (ECO Multi-Layer)"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Nutrition & Wellness", "Industrial", "Personal Care", "Agriculture", "Animal Health", "Cannabis/Hemp/CBD", "Hardware", "Hazardous materials", "Healthcare/Nutra", "Specialty Chemicals"], "materials": ["HDPE", "PET", "Post-consumer recycled (PCR) resin", "Multi-layer co-extrusion materials"], "equipment": ["The Cyclone"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Grand Prairie, Texas -> db", "Extrusion blow-molding manufacturing facilities throughout the United States -> /", "Injection Stretch Blow Molding (ISBM) capabilities -> /", "HDPE and PET containers, PriorityPour tight heads, canisters, dry-pack towel wipes -> /", "GreenLite program with PCR content up to 80% in ECO Multi-Layer products -> /", "Sustainability goals: 60% recycled/renewable materials by 2035, 80% recyclable products by 2028, 30% Scope 2/3 emissions reduction by 2030 -> /", "Industries served: Food & Beverage, Nutrition & Wellness, Industrial, Personal Care, Agriculture, Animal Health, Cann